<title>INDIA: Central Bank of India to post net profit in 96/97.</title>
<headline>Central Bank of India to post net profit in 96/97.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-run Central Bank of India (CBI) said on Thursday it expected to post a net profit for 1996/97 (April-March) after four years of loss, based on provisional results.</p>
<p>The bank recorded a deposit growth of 14.7 percent during the year to 223 billion rupees, CBI said in a statement.</p>
<p>The bank's total advances were 105 billion rupees, it added.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
